{"id":"1477d46205773687","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-df-infinitely-divisible.md","title":"Infinitely Divisible","display":"df-infinitely-divisible — Infinitely Divisible","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-infinitely-divisible","aliases":["58-df-infinitely-divisible"],"display":"df-infinitely-divisible — Infinitely Divisible","depends_on":["[[../batch13/58-df-measure.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-infinitely-divisible"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-infinitely-divisible</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-infinitely-divisible — Infinitely Divisible"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ca832ed6bc22f728\" href=\"?note=ca832ed6bc22f728\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-measure.md\">../batch13/58-df-measure.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(G,+)\">\\((G,+)\\)</span> (locally compact abelian group)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal B(G)\">\\(\\mathcal B(G)\\)</span> (Borel <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma\">\\(\\sigma\\)</span>-algebra)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu\">\\(\\mu\\)</span> (measure on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G\">\\(G\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"*\">\\(*\\)</span> (convolution of measures on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G\">\\(G\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Measure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Measure}_S\\)</span> (measure predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"ca832ed6bc22f728\" href=\"?note=ca832ed6bc22f728\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-measure.md\">../batch13/58-df-measure.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{InfDiv}_G(\\mu)\">\\(\\mathrm{InfDiv}_G(\\mu)\\)</span> (infinitely-divisible probability-measure predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}infinitely-divisible} \\vdash \\mathrm{InfDiv}_G(\\mu) \\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu,G,\\mathcal B(G))\\land\\mu(G)=1\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists\\mu_n\\in[0,\\infty]^{\\mathcal B(G)}\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu_n,G,\\mathcal B(G))\\land\\mu_n(G)=1\\land\\mu=\\mu_n^{*_{G}n}\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}infinitely-divisible} \\vdash \\mathrm{InfDiv}_G(\\mu) \\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu,G,\\mathcal B(G))\\land\\mu(G)=1\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists\\mu_n\\in[0,\\infty]^{\\mathcal B(G)}\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu_n,G,\\mathcal B(G))\\land\\mu_n(G)=1\\land\\mu=\\mu_n^{*_{G}n}\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Every one-time marginal of a Lévy process is infinitely divisible; conversely, on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R^d\">\\(\\mathbb R^d\\)</span> each infinitely divisible law occurs as the time-one law of a Lévy process.</li>\n<li>Normal, Poisson, and stable laws are infinitely divisible.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch13/58-df-measure.md","status":"resolved","id":"ca832ed6bc22f728","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-measure.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-measure.md","status":"resolved","id":"ca832ed6bc22f728","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Measure}_S$ (measure predicate, see [[../batch13/58-df-measure.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"(G,+)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal B(G)","display":false},{"tex":"\\sigma","display":false},{"tex":"\\mu","display":false},{"tex":"G","display":false},{"tex":"*","display":false},{"tex":"G","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Measure}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{InfDiv}_G(\\mu)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}infinitely-divisible} \\vdash \\mathrm{InfDiv}_G(\\mu) \\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu,G,\\mathcal B(G))\\land\\mu(G)=1\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists\\mu_n\\in[0,\\infty]^{\\mathcal B(G)}\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Measure}_S(\\mu_n,G,\\mathcal B(G))\\land\\mu_n(G)=1\\land\\mu=\\mu_n^{*_{G}n}\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathbb R^d","display":false}],"bytes":1247,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-680","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-infinitely-divisible.md|58-df-infinitely-divisible]]（batch07）"}],"outgoing":["ca832ed6bc22f728"]}